<!--
  vaml_ui_tester S640 sample — IMAGE + SOURCE (the driver's explicit FIRST step
  for Sprint 11r). The exact thing that kept failing transparent/black in the
  live viewer: an authored <Image Source="..."/> that must load through the
  S483/S202_1 icon-asset pipeline, be placed at its layout rect, and have its
  quad ACTUALLY drawn on the rendered surface.

  BARE `Source` DP (the S640 headline): pre-S640 only the DOTTED "Image.Source"
  DP was registered, so a BARE `Source="..."` attribute threw
  `unknown property 'Source'`. S640 registers the BARE `Source` DP (the reader
  resolves a bare attribute key by bare name), so `Source="..."` RESOLVES.

  DECLARED EXPECTED OUTCOME (the S641 scanner's oracle — consumed by the
  scanner at S641, declared here per the Sprint 11r contract):
    - element      : Image (the first authored Image under ScanRoot)
    - source       : assets/face-blowing-a-kiss-64.svg  (a REAL rasterized SVG asset)
    - layout rect  : x=32, y=32, w=128, h=128  (the image's arranged box)
    - outcome      : NON-DEFAULT pixels at that rect (the rasterized SVG quad is
                     ACTUALLY drawn — an opaque non-black/non-transparent region,
                     NOT the transparent/black the image kept failing as)
  The scanner (S641) will render this doc through the REAL retained render path,
  scrape the rect for compliance, and compare to this declared outcome.
-->
<StackPanel xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
            x:Name="ScanRoot" Width="440" Height="360" Background="#FF1C1C1C">

  <Image Source="assets/face-blowing-a-kiss-64.svg"
         Width="128" Height="128" Margin="32"/>

</StackPanel>
